From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:39:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] spu: predefine the reference PS3 platform macros

The reference PS3 SPU compiler predefines __CELLOS_LV2__, __LP32__, _LP32,
__STRICT_ALIGNED, __DOUBLE_ACCURATE__ and __FLOAT_FAST__.  Reference
headers and samples select their PS3 code paths on __CELLOS_LV2__; the
accuracy markers describe this back end: IEEE double arithmetic and the
hardware fast single precision.

(Ported to GCC 16 from patches/spu/gcc-9.5.0/0008-spu-reference-predefines.patch.)
---
 gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h b/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h
index 9a5b3585de3..d5f3e1cafb8 100644
--- a/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h
@@ -103,3 +103,11 @@
   "%{mspurs-job:-lspurs_job_runtime} " \
   "%{mspurs-job-initialize:-lspurs_jq_runtime} " \
   SPU_ORDINARY_LIB_SPEC " -lspurs -lsync --end-group; :" SPU_ORDINARY_LIB_SPEC "}"
+
+/* The reference PS3 SPU compiler predefines these; reference headers and
+   samples select their PS3 code paths on __CELLOS_LV2__, and the accuracy
+   markers describe this back end's code generation: IEEE double
+   arithmetic and the hardware's fast single precision.  */
+#undef CPP_SPEC
+#define CPP_SPEC "-D__CELLOS_LV2__ -D__LP32__ -D_LP32 -D__STRICT_ALIGNED " \
+  "-D__DOUBLE_ACCURATE__ -D__FLOAT_FAST__"
